  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "# Explore a Sort\r\n\r\n## Do This:\r\n\r\n1. Click **Highest Rated** and watch how the movie grid changes.\r\n\r\n2. In `script.js`, find `sortHighestRatedMovies()`. Ask AI to help you explain how the movie list, `.sort()`, `return`, and `renderMovies()` work together.\r\n\r\n3. Check that you can explain:\r\n   - which movie property is being compared\r\n   - whether the movies are sorted high → low or low → high\r\n   - how sorting changes the order of movies\r\n   - how sorting is different from filtering\r\n   - how the sorted list gets passed to `renderMovies()`\r\n\r\n4. Above `sortHighestRatedMovies()`, add a `//` comment explaining what the sort does.\r\n\r\nRemember: this level focuses on the **sort → render** part of a pipeline.\r\n\r\nsort → render",
    "submittable": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
